PURPOSE
Extend the existing Kosh Innovations Global Item Creation Portal so authorized
administrators can add new business modules and configure the relevant menus,
pages, features, fields, workflows, permissions, integrations, reports, and
settings from within the portal. This is an additional requirement. Preserve all
previous requirements and existing module functionality. Do not replace or
shorten the existing specification.

CURRENT MODULES
The current first-class business modules are:
1. Item Master
2. Business Partner Master (BP Master)

Treat these as existing registered modules. Do not recreate them or break their
current functionality while introducing the configurable module registry.
Existing module identifiers, records, routes, permissions, settings, data, audit
history, and integrations must be preserved.

CORE REQUIREMENT: ADD NEW MODULE
Create an administrator-only "Module Management" page, preferably under Settings
or Platform Administration, with the ability to:
- View all registered modules and their status.
- Add a new module using a guided wizard.
- Edit the configuration of a module where permitted.
- Enable, disable, suspend, archive, and reactivate a module according to
  controlled lifecycle rules.
- Configure module name, unique machine identifier, description, icon,
  navigation group, display order, owning team, module owner, status, version,
  and dependencies.
- Define the module's menu tree, pages, sub-pages, actions, features, field
  configuration, workflows, approvals, notifications, reports, dashboards,
  import/export options, API integrations, and module settings.
- Preview the navigation and page layout before publishing a module.
- Save a draft, validate configuration, publish, and roll back to a prior
  published configuration version.
- View module version history, who changed it, when, what changed, approval
  status, and audit events.
- Display clear dependency and impact warnings before enabling, disabling,
  archiving, or changing a module.
- Search, sort, and filter the module registry by module name, identifier,
  status, owner, version, and last-updated date.
- Support multiple pages and server-side pagination for a large module registry.

Do not imply that adding a module through metadata alone automatically creates
arbitrary production business logic. The system must distinguish between:
(A) configurable modules assembled from approved reusable platform components,
and
(B) modules that require new custom backend logic, database migrations, external
    integrations, or specialist development.
For case (B), generate a clear implementation checklist and mark unavailable
capabilities as "Not implemented" until actual code, migrations, security checks,
and tests have been completed.

MODULE CREATION WIZARD
Provide a multi-step wizard with save-and-resume capability:

Step 1 — Module identity
