Step 9 — Preview, validation, and publication
Before publishing, run a validation checklist covering:
- Unique module key and route names
- Valid menu/page hierarchy
- Required dependencies
- Component/template compatibility
- Permissions and authorization policy
- Field definitions and supported data types
- Workflow completeness
- Integration configuration and secret references
- Accessibility and responsive layout
- Navigation and broken-link checks
- Migration requirements and schema safety
- Audit coverage
- Security and input validation
- Automated test coverage and acceptance criteria

Show findings by severity: blocking error, warning, or informational message.
Do not publish when blocking errors exist. Allow saving as draft when the
configuration is incomplete. Provide a preview mode that does not execute
production writes, send real messages, or create SAP records.

Step 10 — Approval and activation
Support a controlled lifecycle:
Draft -> Validation -> Pending Approval (when required) -> Published/Disabled
-> Enabled, with explicit transitions and audit history.

Require approval by a separate authorized approver for production publication
